1
00:02:12,360 --> 00:02:14,680
Say , is this the moving-picture ship ?

2
00:02:14,832 --> 00:02:16,632
The Venture ? Yeah .

3
00:02:16,786 --> 00:02:20,186
- Are you going on this crazy voyage ? - What 's crazy about it ?

4
00:02:20,336 --> 00:02:24,216
I don 't know . But everybody is talking about that crazy fella running it .

5
00:02:24,362 --> 00:02:27,002
- Carl Denham ? - Guess that 's the name .

6
00:02:27,155 --> 00:02:30,155
He ain 't scared of nothing . If he wants a picture of lion

7
00:02:30,305 --> 00:02:33,145
he just goes up to him and tells him to look pleasant .

8
00:02:33,336 --> 00:02:36,896
He 's a tough egg . Why all this talk about this voyage being crazy ?

9
00:02:37,044 --> 00:02:41,604
Everybody around the docks is talking about the cargo , for one thing .

10
00:02:41,790 --> 00:02:44,710
And I never did see a ship this size with such a crew .

11
00:02:44,861 --> 00:02:47,541
- Not enough men to handle her ? - Not enough !

12
00:02:47,691 --> 00:02:49,931
Three times more than the ship needs .

13
00:02:50,085 --> 00:02:52,965
I don 't see where they 're gonna have room enough to sleep .

14
00:02:53,115 --> 00:02:55,795
Hey , down there . What do you want ?

15
00:02:55,946 --> 00:02:58,306
- Denham aboard ? - Who are you ?

16
00:02:58,458 --> 00:03:00,378
My name is Weston , the theatrical agent .

17
00:03:00,533 --> 00:03:03,413
Well , why didn 't you say so ? Come on aboard .

18
00:03:04,599 --> 00:03:09,039
Denham 's getting wild . I hope you 've got some good news for him .

19
00:03:10,262 --> 00:03:13,862
Well , Mr. Denham , you know the reasons for hurrying as well as I do .

20
00:03:14,011 --> 00:03:16,371
Insurance company found out we 're carrying explosives .

21
00:03:16,522 --> 00:03:18,762
Marshal will be aboard tomorrow or next day .

22
00:03:18,916 --> 00:03:22,076
If we make a legal case of it , we 'll be tied up for months ?

23
00:03:22,264 --> 00:03:25,224
With enough ammunition to blow up the harbor .

24
00:03:27,130 --> 00:03:30,690
What do you think the marshal will say to these new gas bombs of yours ?

25
00:03:30,839 --> 00:03:34,359
According to you , one of them is enough to knock out an elephant .

26
00:03:34,547 --> 00:03:37,507
We 've got to get where we 're going before the monsoon starts .

27
00:03:37,697 --> 00:03:41,377
- Trust me to see you through a blow . - Oh , now , don 't get sore , skipper .

28
00:03:41,566 --> 00:03:45,566
You can 't run into the rainy season when you 're trying to make an outdoor picture .

29
00:03:45,753 --> 00:03:47,953
Months wasted , money gone and nothing to show .

30
00:03:48,107 --> 00:03:50,107
Still you always bring back a picture .

31
00:03:50,258 --> 00:03:53,978
And everybody says , " There 's only one Carl Denham . "

32
00:03:56,002 --> 00:03:58,122
Weston , I was just going ashore to call you .

33
00:03:58,274 --> 00:04:00,114
If I 'd known that , I would have waited .

34
00:04:00,268 --> 00:04:02,788
This is the skipper . Weston , the theatrical agent .

35
00:04:02,980 --> 00:04:04,940
I guess you met Driscoll , the first mate .

36
00:04:05,094 --> 00:04:07,334
Well , Weston , how about the girl ?

37
00:04:07,487 --> 00:04:09,327
- It can 't be done , Denham . - What ?

38
00:04:09,480 --> 00:04:12,080
It 's got to be done . Now , look here , Weston .

39
00:04:12,272 --> 00:04:14,552
Somebody 's interfered with every girl I try to hire .

40
00:04:14,705 --> 00:04:17,785
Now all the agents in town have shut down on me . All but you .

41
00:04:17,934 --> 00:04:20,734
- You know I 'm square . - Everybody knows you 're square .

42
00:04:20,885 --> 00:04:23,125
But you 've got a reputation for recklessness

43
00:04:23,277 --> 00:04:26,117
that can 't be glossed over . Then you 're so secretive .

44
00:04:26,309 --> 00:04:27,709
You said it .

45
00:04:27,903 --> 00:04:30,863
Even skipper and mate don 't know where they 're going , what .

46
00:04:31,014 --> 00:04:33,494
There you are . I 've got a conscience , Denham .

47
00:04:33,646 --> 00:04:36,926
I can 't send a pretty girl such as you ask on a job like this

48
00:04:37,114 --> 00:04:40,314
without telling her what to expect . - What is she to expect ?

49
00:04:40,466 --> 00:04:43,346
To go off on a trip for no one knows how long

50
00:04:43,534 --> 00:04:46,334
to some spot you don 't even hint at

51
00:04:46,527 --> 00:04:50,527
the only woman on a ship with the toughest mugs I ever looked at .

52
00:04:53,305 --> 00:04:55,345
I mean the crew .

53
00:04:56,655 --> 00:04:59,615
Good Lord , you talk as if I never brought anybody back alive .

54
00:04:59,765 --> 00:05:02,525
The skipper and Driscoll have stuck to me on two trips .

55
00:05:02,676 --> 00:05:05,996
- They look well enough . - Sure , we 're healthy .

56
00:05:06,185 --> 00:05:08,825
But it 's a different thing taking a girl into danger .

57
00:05:09,018 --> 00:05:11,058
I suppose there 's no danger in New York .

58
00:05:11,251 --> 00:05:14,051
Listen , there are dozens of girls in this town

59
00:05:14,242 --> 00:05:16,962
that are in more danger than they are with me .

60
00:05:17,113 --> 00:05:19,793
Yeah , but they know that kind of danger .

61
00:05:19,943 --> 00:05:22,183
You never had a woman in any of your pictures .

62
00:05:22,336 --> 00:05:24,336
- Why do you want one ? - Holy mackerel !

63
00:05:24,489 --> 00:05:26,489
Do you think I wanna haul a woman around ?

64
00:05:26,644 --> 00:05:29,484
- Then why ? - Because the public , bless them

65
00:05:29,633 --> 00:05:31,113
must have a pretty face .

66
00:05:31,309 --> 00:05:34,629
Sure , everybody likes romance .

67
00:05:34,778 --> 00:05:38,778
Isn 't there any romance or adventure without having a flapper in it ?

68
00:05:38,926 --> 00:05:42,086
Well , Mr. Denham , why not take a picture in a monastery ?

69
00:05:42,274 --> 00:05:45,674
Makes me sore . I go out , sweat blood to make a swell picture

70
00:05:45,824 --> 00:05:48,024
then the critics and the exhibitors all say :

71
00:05:48,177 --> 00:05:51,537
" If this picture had love interest , it would gross twice as much . "

72
00:05:51,727 --> 00:05:55,167
The public wants a girl , and this time I 'm gonna give what they want .

73
00:05:55,315 --> 00:05:58,315
- Don 't know where you 'll get her . - I 've gotta get her , Weston .

74
00:05:58,504 --> 00:05:59,864
We 've gotta leave by morning .

75
00:06:00,021 --> 00:06:02,381
- We 've gotta be gone by daylight . - Why ?

76
00:06:02,532 --> 00:06:04,692
Well , there 's a good reason .

77
00:06:04,844 --> 00:06:07,484
Everything I hear about it makes me like it less .

78
00:06:07,638 --> 00:06:09,318
I 'm glad I didn 't get you a girl .

79
00:06:09,472 --> 00:06:11,192
You are , eh ? Well , I 'll show you .

80
00:06:11,384 --> 00:06:14,544
Do you think I 'm gonna give up because you can 't find me a girl ?

81
00:06:14,696 --> 00:06:17,336
I 'm going to make the greatest picture in the world .

82
00:06:17,488 --> 00:06:20,168
Something that nobody 's ever seen or heard of .

83
00:06:20,318 --> 00:06:23,798
They 'll have to think up a lot of new adjectives when I come back .

84
00:06:23,987 --> 00:06:25,627
- Where you going ? - Going out

85
00:06:25,782 --> 00:06:29,742
and get a girl for my picture . Even if I have to marry one .

86
00:06:53,177 --> 00:06:56,537
- Stand aside , please . Get your case later . - Can I take my things ?

87
00:06:59,517 --> 00:07:01,237
Say , lay off the shoving , will you ?

88
00:07:01,392 --> 00:07:03,992
- Oh , I didn 't mean to shove you . - Excuse me .

89
00:07:04,183 --> 00:07:05,943
What do they give you in this joint ?

90
00:07:06,097 --> 00:07:08,817
Soup tonight . Coffee and sinkers in the morning .

91
00:07:28,189 --> 00:07:32,309
I catch you , you stealer . Now , I get you cop . You like that , huh ?

92
00:07:32,456 --> 00:07:35,776
No , no . I didn 't . Let me go . I wanted to , but I didn 't .

93
00:07:35,926 --> 00:07:38,846
- Had enough of these stealers . - Dry up . Kid didn 't take any .

94
00:07:38,996 --> 00:07:41,236
- Truly I didn 't . - Three people this week ...

95
00:07:41,429 --> 00:07:42,909
- Here ... Here 's a buck . - A buck .

96
00:07:43,064 --> 00:07:44,624
Scram .

97
00:07:53,113 --> 00:07:55,993
Hey , taxi !

98
00:08:10,139 --> 00:08:12,099
Feeling better ?

99
00:08:12,255 --> 00:08:14,215
Yes , thank you .

100
00:08:14,366 --> 00:08:17,166
- You 're very kind . - Don 't you fool yourself .

101
00:08:17,319 --> 00:08:20,759
I 'm not bothering about you just out of kindness .

102
00:08:24,376 --> 00:08:27,736
- How 'd you ever get into this fix ? - Bad luck , I guess .

103
00:08:27,885 --> 00:08:29,565
There are a lot of girls like me .

104
00:08:29,760 --> 00:08:34,400
- Not many with your looks . - I can get by in good clothes all right .

105
00:08:34,546 --> 00:08:37,546
- But when a girl gets too shabby ... - No family ?

106
00:08:37,695 --> 00:08:39,495
Supposed to have an uncle someplace .

107
00:08:40,448 --> 00:08:42,728
Did you ever do any acting ?

108
00:08:42,879 --> 00:08:45,919
I used to do extra work now and then over on Long Island .

109
00:08:46,070 --> 00:08:47,870
The studio 's closed now .

110
00:08:48,064 --> 00:08:50,624
- What 's your name ? - Ann Darrow .

111
00:08:50,814 --> 00:08:52,814
Fine . I 've got a job for you .

112
00:08:53,767 --> 00:08:55,327
Costumes on the ship will fit you .

113
00:08:55,481 --> 00:08:58,121
If the shops are still open , I can get clothes for you .

114
00:08:58,313 --> 00:08:59,753
- Come on . - But ...

115
00:08:59,907 --> 00:09:03,187
- But what is it ? - It 's money and adventure and fame .

116
00:09:03,338 --> 00:09:05,858
It 's the thrill of a lifetime . A long sea voyage

117
00:09:06,047 --> 00:09:08,487
that starts at 6 : 00 tomorrow morning .

118
00:09:08,640 --> 00:09:10,400
No , wait .

119
00:09:11,591 --> 00:09:13,711
I don 't understand . You must tell me .

120
00:09:13,904 --> 00:09:16,744
I do want the job so

121
00:09:17,133 --> 00:09:19,333
but I can 't . - Oh , I see .

122
00:09:19,528 --> 00:09:22,568
No , you 've got me wrong . This is strictly business .

123
00:09:25,030 --> 00:09:27,550
- I only wanted ... - Sure . Sure you did .

124
00:09:27,743 --> 00:09:30,583
I got a little excited and I forgot you didn 't understand .

125
00:09:32,247 --> 00:09:36,127
Listen , I 'm Carl Denham . Ever heard of me ?

126
00:09:36,275 --> 00:09:39,995
Yes , yes . You make moving pictures in jungles and places .

127
00:09:40,184 --> 00:09:42,824
That 's right . And I pick you as lead in my next picture .

128
00:09:43,015 --> 00:09:45,215
We sail at 6 .

129
00:09:45,368 --> 00:09:48,248
- Where to ? - A long way off .

130
00:09:48,399 --> 00:09:52,959
And listen , Ann , I 'm on the level . No funny business .

131
00:09:54,101 --> 00:09:59,461
- What do I have to do ? - Just trust me and keep your chin up .

132
00:10:16,352 --> 00:10:18,752
Hey , you men on that winch

133
00:10:18,945 --> 00:10:21,905
down below on the deck and help with these hatches .

134
00:10:29,751 --> 00:10:32,391
Hurry this line forward .

135
00:10:32,583 --> 00:10:35,743
Forward , you farmer and up here !

136
00:10:35,932 --> 00:10:37,572
What are you doing up here ?

137
00:10:37,726 --> 00:10:40,686
- I just wanted to see . - Oh , you just wanted to see .

138
00:10:40,837 --> 00:10:43,677
Well , I 'm sorry . Make that line fast !

139
00:10:43,828 --> 00:10:45,948
You 're that girl Denham picked , aren 't you ?

140
00:10:46,100 --> 00:10:49,980
Yes . I think this is awfully exciting . I 've never been on a ship before .

141
00:10:50,128 --> 00:10:52,248
I 've never been on one with a woman before .

142
00:10:53,080 --> 00:10:55,720
I guess you don 't think much of women on ships ?

143
00:10:55,871 --> 00:10:57,991
No , they 're a nuisance .

144
00:10:58,183 --> 00:11:01,063
- I 'll try not to be . - You 've been in the way already .

145
00:11:01,254 --> 00:11:03,894
Bring that ladder aboard !

146
00:11:04,445 --> 00:11:05,885
Well , you better stay below .

147
00:11:06,359 --> 00:11:08,559
What ? The whole voyage ?

148
00:11:10,268 --> 00:11:12,588
I 'm afraid I didn 't apologize for hitting you .

149
00:11:12,739 --> 00:11:15,139
That was a pretty tough rap on the chin .

150
00:11:23,866 --> 00:11:26,826
- Well , we 're off . - We 're off .

151
00:11:40,095 --> 00:11:43,335
Say , how many potatoes do you think you 've peeled in six weeks ?

152
00:11:43,484 --> 00:11:44,804
Too many .

153
00:11:44,999 --> 00:11:47,319
Sailors eat an awful lot , don 't they ?

154
00:11:47,472 --> 00:11:49,952
All time eat . Someday me go back China .

155
00:11:50,143 --> 00:11:51,423
Never see no more potatoes .

156
00:11:53,654 --> 00:11:56,814
- Charlie , isn 't the ocean wonderful ? - Very pretty .

157
00:11:57,003 --> 00:12:00,083
Pretty soon you be all same sailor , only no eat so much .

158
00:12:00,233 --> 00:12:03,393
I 'd like to be . Only , of course , it wasn 't so nice up north

159
00:12:03,543 --> 00:12:05,783
when it was cold and rough was it ?

160
00:12:05,936 --> 00:12:10,656
Ocean very nice when you order weather or some eggs for breakfast .

161
00:12:14,907 --> 00:12:17,187
- Hello , Ann . - Hello , Jack .

162
00:12:17,341 --> 00:12:18,701
Where you been all morning ?

163
00:12:18,896 --> 00:12:20,456
Trying on costumes for Mr. Denham .

164
00:12:20,651 --> 00:12:22,931
He 's gonna make some tests of me here on deck

165
00:12:23,122 --> 00:12:25,802
if the light is right . - Tests , why ?

166
00:12:26,712 --> 00:12:31,472
Oh , to see which side of my face looks best and all that .

167
00:12:31,616 --> 00:12:34,296
Both sides look all right to me .

168
00:12:34,488 --> 00:12:37,248
Yes , but you 're not the movie director .

169
00:12:37,398 --> 00:12:40,198
If I was , you wouldn 't be here .

170
00:12:40,749 --> 00:12:43,749
Well , is that a nice thing to say .

171
00:12:43,940 --> 00:12:46,380
This is no place for a girl .

172
00:12:46,571 --> 00:12:50,371
I wish you wouldn 't keep harping on that . It 's very mean of you .

173
00:12:50,519 --> 00:12:53,839
Anybody would think I 'd been a lot of trouble .

174
00:12:53,987 --> 00:12:58,787
I haven 't . You can 't say I 've been one bit of trouble to anyone

175
00:12:59,173 --> 00:13:00,773
have I ?

176
00:13:00,926 --> 00:13:03,486
- Sure you have . Sure you have . - I don 't see ...

177
00:13:03,638 --> 00:13:05,598
Well , how ?

178
00:13:05,752 --> 00:13:08,152
Just ... Just being around is trouble .

179
00:13:08,544 --> 00:13:12,224
Oh , dear , and I thought everything was going so nicely .

180
00:13:12,371 --> 00:13:13,931
Oh , you 're all right .

181
00:13:14,086 --> 00:13:17,086
But women just can 't help being a bother .

182
00:13:17,236 --> 00:13:20,196
- Made that way I guess . - Well , anyhow ...

183
00:13:21,264 --> 00:13:25,144
I 've had the happiest time of my life on this old ship .

184
00:13:25,291 --> 00:13:27,251
That 's ... That 's fine .

185
00:13:32,868 --> 00:13:34,228
Say ...

186
00:13:34,383 --> 00:13:35,863
Did you really mean that , Ann ?

187
00:13:36,019 --> 00:13:40,819
Of course . Everyone 's so nice to me . Dr. Denham and the skipper ...

188
00:13:40,963 --> 00:13:44,843
Don 't you think the skipper is a sweet old lamb ?

189
00:13:45,270 --> 00:13:47,510
I 'd hate to have him hear me say that .

190
00:13:47,661 --> 00:13:49,341
Iggy 's nice to me .

191
00:13:49,538 --> 00:13:53,138
Iggy likes me better than he likes anybody onboard .

192
00:13:53,325 --> 00:13:55,365
Don 't you , Iggy ?

193
00:13:57,990 --> 00:14:01,510
- That 's right . Of course you do . - Beauty and the beast , eh ?

194
00:14:01,659 --> 00:14:04,139
Well , now , I never thought I was good-looking .

195
00:14:04,331 --> 00:14:07,531
Put on one of the costumes . The light 's right for those tests now .

196
00:14:07,681 --> 00:14:11,601
All right , Mr. Denham . I won 't be a minute .

197
00:14:11,749 --> 00:14:14,389
Beauty and the beast .

198
00:14:14,540 --> 00:14:16,700
Mr. Denham

199
00:14:16,853 --> 00:14:18,573
I 'm gonna do some butting in .

200
00:14:18,726 --> 00:14:20,886
- What 's your trouble ? - When do we find out

201
00:14:21,040 --> 00:14:22,720
where we 're going ? - Pretty soon .

202
00:14:22,874 --> 00:14:24,554
Will you tell us what happens after ?

203
00:14:24,709 --> 00:14:27,669
How can I ? I 'm not a fortuneteller .

204
00:14:27,819 --> 00:14:29,819
You must have some idea what you 're after .

205
00:14:30,012 --> 00:14:31,612
What 's the matter ? You going soft .

206
00:14:31,767 --> 00:14:34,967
Oh , you know I 'm not . Not for myself .

207
00:14:35,116 --> 00:14:37,916
- For Ann . - Oh , you have gone soft on her , eh ?

208
00:14:38,108 --> 00:14:41,588
I 've got enough troubles without a love affair to complicate things .

209
00:14:41,737 --> 00:14:45,017
- Better cut it out , Jack . - Love affair .

210
00:14:45,166 --> 00:14:48,086
- Think I 'm gonna fall for any dame ? - I never knew it to fail .

211
00:14:48,236 --> 00:14:51,276
Some big hard-boiled egg gets a look at a pretty face , bang

212
00:14:51,466 --> 00:14:53,706
he cracks up , gets sappy . - Who 's going sappy ?

213
00:14:53,858 --> 00:14:55,258
I haven 't run out on you ?

214
00:14:55,415 --> 00:14:57,215
No . You 're a pretty tough guy .

215
00:14:57,367 --> 00:14:59,967
But if beauty gets you , you ...

216
00:15:01,556 --> 00:15:04,636
I 'm going right into a theme song here .

217
00:15:05,105 --> 00:15:09,345
- Say , what are you talking about ? - It 's the idea of my picture .

218
00:15:09,491 --> 00:15:11,411
The beast was a tough guy too .

219
00:15:11,565 --> 00:15:15,805
He could lick the world , but when he saw beauty , she got him .

220
00:15:15,950 --> 00:15:19,830
He went soft , he forgot his wisdom and the little fellas licked him .

221
00:15:20,019 --> 00:15:21,419
Think it over , Jack .

222
00:15:21,574 --> 00:15:23,814
Mr. Denham , skipper wants you up on the bridge .

223
00:15:24,007 --> 00:15:26,167
- He says we 've reached the position . - Good .

224
00:15:26,319 --> 00:15:29,199
Come on , Jack . You 're in on this . I 'm gonna spill it .

225
00:15:31,065 --> 00:15:35,025
There 's our noon position . Two south , 90 east .

226
00:15:35,572 --> 00:15:38,052
Now , you promised some information when we got here .

227
00:15:38,243 --> 00:15:41,843
- Way west of Sumatra . - And way out of any waters I know .

228
00:15:41,992 --> 00:15:44,232
I know the East Indies like I do my own hand

229
00:15:44,383 --> 00:15:47,063
but I 've never been here . - Where do we go from here ?

230
00:15:47,255 --> 00:15:48,895
- Southwest . - Southwest ?

231
00:15:49,090 --> 00:15:51,450
Well , there is nothing for thousands of miles .

232
00:15:51,601 --> 00:15:54,681
Keep your shirt on , skipper . We 're not going thousands of miles .

233
00:15:54,833 --> 00:15:57,433
Here 's the island we 're looking for .

234
00:15:58,939 --> 00:16:01,659
Well , that position . Let 's have the big chart .

235
00:16:01,810 --> 00:16:03,770
You won 't find that island on any chart .

236
00:16:03,924 --> 00:16:06,684
That was made by the skipper of a Norwegian bark .

237
00:16:06,835 --> 00:16:09,235
- He must have been kidding . - No , he wasn 't .

238
00:16:09,387 --> 00:16:13,707
Listen , a canoe full of natives from this island was blown to sea .

239
00:16:13,852 --> 00:16:16,172
When the bark picked them , there was one alive .

240
00:16:16,364 --> 00:16:19,204
He died before they reached port , not before the skipper

241
00:16:19,355 --> 00:16:22,795
had a description of the island and got an idea of where it lies .

242
00:16:22,947 --> 00:16:25,347
- Where did you get it ? - Singapore , two years ago .

243
00:16:25,498 --> 00:16:27,058
Skipper knew I 'd be interested .

244
00:16:27,212 --> 00:16:30,532
- Does he believe it ? - I don 't know . But I do .

245
00:16:30,682 --> 00:16:34,122
Here . Here 's what the island looks like .

246
00:16:37,859 --> 00:16:39,699
There 's a long , sandy peninsula .

247
00:16:39,853 --> 00:16:42,613
The only possible landing place is through this reef .

248
00:16:42,764 --> 00:16:45,644
Rest of shoreline 's sheer precipice , hundreds of feet high .

249
00:16:45,795 --> 00:16:48,435
And across the base of the peninsula , cutting it off

250
00:16:48,586 --> 00:16:51,066
from the rest of the island , is a wall .

251
00:16:51,617 --> 00:16:54,857
- A wall ? - Built long ago . People who lived there

252
00:16:55,006 --> 00:16:58,086
slipped back , forgotten the high civilization that built it .

253
00:16:58,278 --> 00:17:00,798
That wall is as strong today as it was centuries ago .

254
00:17:00,949 --> 00:17:03,429
The natives keep that wall in repair .

255
00:17:03,581 --> 00:17:05,581
- They need it . - Why ?

256
00:17:05,734 --> 00:17:09,254
There 's something on the other side of it . Something they fear .

257
00:17:09,443 --> 00:17:11,643
A hostile tribe .

258
00:17:18,375 --> 00:17:21,535
Did you ever hear of Kong ?

259
00:17:23,639 --> 00:17:25,559
Why , yes .

260
00:17:25,713 --> 00:17:29,473
Some native superstition , isn 't it ? A god or a spirit or something .

261
00:17:30,019 --> 00:17:32,579
Well , anyway , neither beast nor man

262
00:17:32,732 --> 00:17:35,772
something monstrous , all-powerful .

263
00:17:36,160 --> 00:17:37,480
Still living

264
00:17:37,635 --> 00:17:41,195
still holding that island in a grip of deadly fear .

265
00:17:44,456 --> 00:17:46,696
Well , every legend has a basis of truth .

266
00:17:46,847 --> 00:17:50,727
I tell you , there 's something on that island that no white man has ever seen .

267
00:17:50,876 --> 00:17:55,036
- And you expect to photograph it ? - If it 's there , you bet I 'll photograph it .

268
00:17:55,899 --> 00:17:58,539
Suppose it doesn 't like having its picture taken ?

269
00:18:00,604 --> 00:18:04,884
Well , now you know why I brought along those cases of gas bombs .

270
00:18:11,690 --> 00:18:14,930
Oh , you 've put on a beauty-and-beast costume , eh ?

271
00:18:15,081 --> 00:18:17,001
It 's the prettiest .

272
00:18:17,154 --> 00:18:20,154
All right . Just stand right over there .

273
00:18:21,462 --> 00:18:24,902
I 'm sort of nervous . Suppose I don 't photograph well ?

274
00:18:25,050 --> 00:18:28,130
You don 't have to worry about that . If I hadn 't been sure

275
00:18:28,280 --> 00:18:30,960
I wouldn 't have brought you around the world .

276
00:18:31,191 --> 00:18:34,551
- What will I do ? - Well , we start with the profile .

277
00:18:34,700 --> 00:18:36,380
When I start cranking

278
00:18:36,534 --> 00:18:39,454
why , hold it a minute , and then turn slowly toward me .

279
00:18:39,605 --> 00:18:43,165
You see me . You smile a little , then you listen .

280
00:18:43,354 --> 00:18:46,074
Then you laugh . All right .

281
00:18:46,224 --> 00:18:47,784
Camera .

282
00:18:57,948 --> 00:19:00,668
- Looks kind of silly , don 't it ? - Pretty dame , huh ?

283
00:19:00,860 --> 00:19:02,940
You think maybe he like to take my picture ?

284
00:19:03,093 --> 00:19:06,413
Them cameras cost money . Shouldn 't think he 'd risk it .

285
00:19:08,316 --> 00:19:11,316
Now , that 's fine , Ann . Now we 'll try one with a filter , eh ?

286
00:19:11,906 --> 00:19:13,906
Do you always take the pictures yourself ?

287
00:19:14,538 --> 00:19:16,498
Ever since a trip I made to Africa .

288
00:19:16,652 --> 00:19:19,252
I 'd have got a swell picture of a charging rhino

289
00:19:19,403 --> 00:19:20,923
but the cameraman got scared .

290
00:19:21,117 --> 00:19:23,717
The darned fool . I was right there with a rifle .

291
00:19:23,909 --> 00:19:26,869
Seems he didn 't trust me to get the rhino before it got him .

292
00:19:27,020 --> 00:19:30,460
I haven 't fooled with a cameramen since . I do it myself .

293
00:19:30,609 --> 00:19:33,569
- Think he 's crazy , skipper ? - Just enthusiastic .

294
00:19:33,959 --> 00:19:35,759
Ann , in this one you 're looking down .

295
00:19:35,952 --> 00:19:38,912
When I start to crank , you look up slowly .

296
00:19:39,063 --> 00:19:41,983
You 're quite calm . You don 't expect to see a thing .

297
00:19:42,134 --> 00:19:45,574
Then you just follow my directions . All right ?

298
00:19:46,839 --> 00:19:50,359
Camera . Look up slowly , Ann .

299
00:19:50,547 --> 00:19:53,707
That 's it . You don 't see anything .

300
00:19:53,858 --> 00:19:56,018
Now look higher

301
00:19:56,210 --> 00:19:58,650
still higher .

302
00:19:58,841 --> 00:20:02,401
Now you see it . You 're amazed .

303
00:20:02,550 --> 00:20:06,470
You can 't believe it . Your eyes open wider .

304
00:20:06,658 --> 00:20:09,178
It 's horrible , Ann , but you can 't look away .

305
00:20:09,329 --> 00:20:11,609
There 's no chance for you , Ann , no escape .

306
00:20:11,761 --> 00:20:13,681
You 're helpless , Ann , helpless .

307
00:20:13,876 --> 00:20:16,556
There 's just one chance , if you can scream

308
00:20:16,708 --> 00:20:20,588
but your throat 's paralyzed . Try to scream , Ann , try .

309
00:20:20,735 --> 00:20:23,055
Perhaps if you didn 't see it , you could scream .

310
00:20:23,207 --> 00:20:27,607
Throw your arm across your eyes and scream . Scream for your life .

311
00:20:31,102 --> 00:20:33,862
What 's he think she 's really gonna see ?

312
00:20:49,286 --> 00:20:52,926
This infernal fog . Sure of your position , skipper ?

313
00:20:53,075 --> 00:20:55,875
Last night before this fog shut down , I got a good sight .

314
00:20:56,027 --> 00:20:57,787
We should be near the island .

315
00:20:58,140 --> 00:21:00,780
If we don 't see it when this fog lifts , we never will .

316
00:21:00,930 --> 00:21:02,370
We 've quartered these parts .

317
00:21:02,846 --> 00:21:04,526
Can 't see your hand in front of your face .

318
00:21:04,679 --> 00:21:07,639
Hey , Charlie , I wish you 'd make your soup as thick as this .

319
00:21:11,339 --> 00:21:14,339
No bottom at 30 .

320
00:21:14,488 --> 00:21:17,608
The Norwegian skipper must 've been guessing at the position .

321
00:21:17,759 --> 00:21:19,399
How will we know it 's the right island ?

322
00:21:19,554 --> 00:21:23,834
- The mountain that looks like a skull . - Oh , yes , I 'd forgotten . You told me .

323
00:21:23,980 --> 00:21:27,100
- Skull Mountain . - By the deep 20 .

324
00:21:27,290 --> 00:21:29,610
Shallowing fast . Mr. Briggs , dead slow .

325
00:21:29,762 --> 00:21:31,722
Dead slow , sir .

326
00:21:31,875 --> 00:21:35,555
- Confound this fog . - By the deep 16 .

327
00:21:35,744 --> 00:21:38,664
- What 'd she draw , skipper ? - Four .

328
00:21:38,815 --> 00:21:40,975
Why don 't he heave to until it clears ?

329
00:21:41,127 --> 00:21:44,807
'Tain 't the old man . It 's that crazy guy , Denham .

330
00:21:45,075 --> 00:21:47,955
Listen , you hear anything ?

331
00:21:48,145 --> 00:21:49,985
No .

332
00:21:50,179 --> 00:21:54,579
- Breakers ahead . - Let go .

333
00:21:59,949 --> 00:22:03,749
That 's not breakers . That 's drums .

334
00:22:22,002 --> 00:22:24,482
Skipper , now the fog 's lifted , do you see anybody ?

335
00:22:24,633 --> 00:22:27,633
- Not a living thing . - Funny they haven 't spotted us .

336
00:22:28,023 --> 00:22:31,303
I 'd think the whole population would be on the beach .

337
00:22:31,893 --> 00:22:33,493
Listen .

338
00:22:38,033 --> 00:22:41,433
Maybe they have spotted us and are signaling .

339
00:22:41,583 --> 00:22:44,663
Well , skipper , do you believe me now ? There it is .

340
00:22:45,051 --> 00:22:46,651
Skull Mountain , the wall .

341
00:22:46,806 --> 00:22:48,966
Everything just like on my funny little map .

342
00:22:49,159 --> 00:22:51,599
- Come on . Let 's get started . - All right .

343
00:22:51,751 --> 00:22:53,991
Twelve men go with you . The rest stay aboard .

344
00:22:54,144 --> 00:22:57,304
Have you got a good man with those gas bombs ?

345
00:22:57,454 --> 00:22:59,014
I think you better go along .

346
00:22:59,169 --> 00:23:01,249
You may be able to talk to these birds .

347
00:23:01,402 --> 00:23:02,922
All right . Mr. Adams .

348
00:23:03,076 --> 00:23:04,796
Aye , sir .

349
00:23:05,231 --> 00:23:07,471
- You 'll take charge of the ship . - Aye , aye , sir .

350
00:23:07,622 --> 00:23:10,782
- I 'm going ashore with you , aren 't I ? - You bet .

351
00:23:10,933 --> 00:23:13,333
I don 't think she should until we know what 's there .

352
00:23:13,484 --> 00:23:15,284
Wait a minute . Who 's running this show ?

353
00:23:15,438 --> 00:23:18,598
I found out from experience to keep my cast and cameras with me .

354
00:23:19,109 --> 00:23:20,749
You never can tell when you 'll want them .

355
00:23:20,902 --> 00:23:22,582
- But you 're crazy to risk ... - Jack

356
00:23:22,736 --> 00:23:25,176
run along and get the rifles and ammunition .

357
00:23:25,328 --> 00:23:27,808
And get me a couple of huskies to carry my stuff .

358
00:23:27,959 --> 00:23:30,039
And , Jack , don 't forget the costume box .

359
00:23:30,233 --> 00:23:33,633
If we 're lucky enough , we may get a swell shot right away .

360
00:23:33,782 --> 00:23:35,342
Come on , Ann .

361
00:23:38,727 --> 00:23:40,927
All right , boys , let 's go .

362
00:23:41,079 --> 00:23:43,359
- Take it easy with that camera . - Okay .

363
00:23:43,512 --> 00:23:45,912
- Plenty of ammunition for those guns ? - Yes , sir .

364
00:23:46,104 --> 00:23:48,064
Be careful with those bombs .

365
00:23:48,218 --> 00:23:51,098
All right , Briggs , now we 'll get a look at Denham 's island .

366
00:23:52,605 --> 00:23:55,125
Stand by to lower away .

367
00:24:28,494 --> 00:24:30,134
You with the camera , stick close .

368
00:24:30,288 --> 00:24:31,808
- Okay . - Who 's got the bombs ?

369
00:24:32,003 --> 00:24:33,443
- I have , sir . - Watch your step .

370
00:24:33,638 --> 00:24:36,198
There 's enough trichloride to put hippos to sleep .

371
00:24:36,391 --> 00:24:37,951
Aye , aye , sir .

372
00:24:38,105 --> 00:24:41,905
- What queer-looking boats . - Yeah , outrigger canoes .

373
00:24:42,292 --> 00:24:44,972
Driscoll , I want two men left here to guard the boat .

374
00:24:45,124 --> 00:24:46,964
- All attended to , sir . - Good .

375
00:24:47,118 --> 00:24:50,238
We all ready , then ? Come on .

376
00:24:59,957 --> 00:25:01,717
Not a soul in sight .

377
00:25:01,871 --> 00:25:03,751
The people must all be gathered up ahead .

378
00:25:03,945 --> 00:25:06,025
That wall , skipper . What do you think of that ?

379
00:25:06,178 --> 00:25:08,818
Colossal . It might almost be Egyptian .

380
00:25:08,969 --> 00:25:11,729
But what 's on the other side of that wall ? I wanna know .

381
00:25:11,921 --> 00:25:14,361
Who do you suppose could have built it ?

382
00:25:14,513 --> 00:25:16,513
Oh , I was up on Angkor once .

383
00:25:16,706 --> 00:25:19,626
That 's bigger than this , and nobody knows who built it .

384
00:25:19,777 --> 00:25:23,337
Oh , boy , what a chance . What a picture .

385
00:25:32,299 --> 00:25:34,059
Come on .

386
00:25:38,199 --> 00:25:41,279
Hear that ? They 're saying , " Kong , Kong . "

387
00:25:41,430 --> 00:25:43,230
Hope you talk their lingo , skipper .

388
00:25:43,383 --> 00:25:45,783
- You catch any words yet ? - I 'm not sure .

389
00:25:45,935 --> 00:25:48,855
Sounds something like the language Nias Islanders speak .

390
00:25:49,008 --> 00:25:50,568
What do you suppose is happening ?

391
00:25:50,721 --> 00:25:52,841
They 're up to some of their heathen tricks .

392
00:25:52,994 --> 00:25:54,634
But don 't go rushing out to sea .

393
00:25:54,788 --> 00:25:57,548
- All right . But isn 't it exciting ? - Sure .

394
00:25:57,700 --> 00:26:01,300
- I wish we 'd left you on the ship . - Oh , I 'm so glad you didn 't .

395
00:26:01,488 --> 00:26:05,008
Wait . Easy , now . Wait till I see what goes on .

396
00:26:17,358 --> 00:26:19,798
Holy mackerel ! What a show .

397
00:26:19,951 --> 00:26:23,631
Hey , skipper , come here and get a load of this .

398
00:26:25,255 --> 00:26:28,135
Did you ever see anything like that before in your life ?

399
00:27:13,508 --> 00:27:16,188
Boy , if I could only get a picture before they see us .

400
00:27:16,338 --> 00:27:19,058
Hey , you with the camera . Come here .

401
00:27:20,166 --> 00:27:22,006
I wanna see .

402
00:27:22,160 --> 00:27:24,920
Come on , but be careful .

403
00:27:48,161 --> 00:27:50,361
- Too late . They see us . - Let 's ... Let 's beat it .

404
00:27:50,513 --> 00:27:53,713
- Hey , what are you running for ? - No use trying to hide now .

405
00:27:53,864 --> 00:27:56,344
Everybody come out in plain sight .

406
00:28:31,228 --> 00:28:34,948
- Say , let 's scram out of here . - Stand still , you fool .

407
00:28:35,136 --> 00:28:37,816
Steady , boys , bluff them .

408
00:28:48,774 --> 00:28:51,934
Come on , skipper . Make him a friendly speech .

409
00:29:10,188 --> 00:29:12,628
He understands you , skipper . What 's he say ?

410
00:29:12,781 --> 00:29:15,781
- He 's telling us to get out . - Well , talk him out of it .

411
00:29:15,931 --> 00:29:18,091
Ask him what goes on .

412
00:29:30,326 --> 00:29:32,486
He says the girl there is the bride of Kong .

413
00:29:32,680 --> 00:29:35,320
Great . Find out what they 're gonna do .

414
00:29:46,915 --> 00:29:49,635
- What 's that ? - He must be the witch doctor .

415
00:29:49,787 --> 00:29:52,467
He says the ceremony is spoiled because we 've seen it .

416
00:29:52,618 --> 00:29:55,618
Well , calm the old boy down . What 's the word for friend ?

417
00:30:06,615 --> 00:30:09,255
Steady with those rifles , boys .

418
00:30:15,786 --> 00:30:19,626
- What 's that ? - He says , look at the golden woman .

419
00:30:19,773 --> 00:30:22,013
Yeah . Blonds are scarce around here .

420
00:30:30,382 --> 00:30:33,862
- A gift for Kong , he says . - Good Lord !

421
00:30:37,720 --> 00:30:39,720
Wants to buy her .

422
00:30:45,615 --> 00:30:48,575
He 's offering to trade six of his women for Ann .

423
00:30:50,202 --> 00:30:52,282
You got her into this , Denham .

424
00:31:03,042 --> 00:31:04,762
I 'm gonna take her back to the ship .

425
00:31:04,954 --> 00:31:07,834
We 'd better get out of here before they think to cut us off .

426
00:31:08,026 --> 00:31:10,986
Guess so . But tell him we 'll be back tomorrow to make friends .

427
00:31:16,838 --> 00:31:21,278
Get going , Ann . Don 't be scared . Everything 's all right .

428
00:31:22,302 --> 00:31:24,742
Smile , Ann , and talk to Jack .

429
00:31:24,894 --> 00:31:26,654
Keep your chin up .

430
00:31:50,097 --> 00:31:54,777
- Say , why aren 't you in bed ? - Oh , I can 't sleep .

431
00:31:54,923 --> 00:31:58,683
The sound of those drums makes me nervous , I guess .

432
00:31:58,829 --> 00:32:01,789
I think Denham 's off his nut taking you ashore today .

433
00:32:01,941 --> 00:32:03,341
Well , I was a little scared .

434
00:32:04,771 --> 00:32:09,051
- I guess you weren 't the only one . - I wonder what we do next .

435
00:32:09,197 --> 00:32:10,797
That 's just what 's worrying me .

436
00:32:10,952 --> 00:32:13,672
Denham 's a fool , there 's no telling what he might

437
00:32:13,824 --> 00:32:15,584
ask you to do for this picture .

438
00:32:15,737 --> 00:32:18,297
After all he 's done , I would take any chance for him .

439
00:32:18,450 --> 00:32:20,090
Don 't talk like that .

440
00:32:20,244 --> 00:32:22,604
I 'd say he 's crazy enough to try anything .

441
00:32:22,755 --> 00:32:25,315
Well , I won 't go back on him .

442
00:32:25,668 --> 00:32:30,028
When I think of what might 've happened today , if anything had happened to you ...

443
00:32:30,214 --> 00:32:32,974
Then you wouldn 't be bothered having a woman onboard .

444
00:32:33,164 --> 00:32:36,844
Don 't laugh . I 'm scared for you .

445
00:32:36,992 --> 00:32:41,032
I 'm sort of ... Well , I 'm scared of you too .

446
00:32:41,220 --> 00:32:42,780
Ann ...

447
00:32:43,773 --> 00:32:45,093
I ...

448
00:32:48,936 --> 00:32:50,816
Say ...

449
00:32:50,970 --> 00:32:53,930
I guess I love you .

450
00:32:54,081 --> 00:32:57,161
Why , Jack , you hate women .

451
00:32:57,869 --> 00:33:00,789
Yeah , I know . But you aren 't women .

452
00:33:02,655 --> 00:33:04,535
Say , Ann ...

453
00:33:04,688 --> 00:33:07,208
I don 't suppose ...

454
00:33:07,400 --> 00:33:09,320
I mean ...

455
00:33:09,473 --> 00:33:13,553
Well , you don 't feel anything like that about me

456
00:33:14,220 --> 00:33:16,020
do you ?

457
00:33:23,271 --> 00:33:25,671
Mr. Driscoll , are you on deck ?

458
00:33:27,858 --> 00:33:29,698
Yes , sir .

459
00:33:30,847 --> 00:33:32,887
Will you please come up on the bridge ?

460
00:33:35,395 --> 00:33:37,555
You go on . I 'll wait here .

461
00:33:41,694 --> 00:33:43,294
Yes , sir .

462
00:34:59,534 --> 00:35:01,174
There , that 's about it .

463
00:35:01,329 --> 00:35:03,729
We 'll make absolutely sure tomorrow noon .

464
00:35:03,882 --> 00:35:06,842
Oh , must be almost midnight .

465
00:35:06,991 --> 00:35:08,991
Hey .

466
00:35:09,146 --> 00:35:10,906
Look at that .

467
00:35:11,059 --> 00:35:13,259
Torches going through the village .

468
00:35:13,612 --> 00:35:17,052
Yeah , looks like the night before election .

469
00:35:17,201 --> 00:35:19,761
Listen to them . Wonder what 's up .

470
00:35:22,186 --> 00:35:24,106
Wish I could take pictures by firelight .

471
00:35:24,259 --> 00:35:27,099
- I 'd sneak ashore and get a scene now . - Oh , be sensible .

472
00:35:27,250 --> 00:35:29,410
We 're lucky to be all safe aboard tonight .

473
00:35:29,603 --> 00:35:31,603
Yeah , I guess so .

474
00:35:38,814 --> 00:35:41,934
- Charlie , have you seen missy ? - Me no see one , two hours .

475
00:35:42,085 --> 00:35:45,245
When we leave this place ? Me no like .

476
00:35:53,449 --> 00:35:55,249
Ann .

477
00:35:55,404 --> 00:35:57,244
Ann .

478
00:36:13,468 --> 00:36:15,468
All hands on deck ! Everybody on deck !

479
00:36:15,620 --> 00:36:17,860
Everybody on deck ! All hands on deck !

480
00:36:18,014 --> 00:36:20,934
Everybody on deck ! Everybody on deck !

481
00:36:21,084 --> 00:36:23,724
- What 's the matter ? What 's happening ? - What 's going on ?

482
00:36:25,192 --> 00:36:27,272
- What 's the matter ? - I 'm out here .

483
00:36:35,361 --> 00:36:36,841
Look , sir . Me find on deck .

484
00:36:36,995 --> 00:36:39,795
- A native bracelet . - Crazy black man been here .

485
00:36:40,305 --> 00:36:41,745
What is it ? Who turned out the crew ?

486
00:36:41,901 --> 00:36:43,941
- Look . Someone 's been aboard . - Where 's Ann ?

487
00:36:44,093 --> 00:36:47,053
- In her cabin . - No , she isn 't . I just looked .

488
00:36:47,324 --> 00:36:50,724
- What 's the matter , Mr. Driscoll ? - Search the ship . Find Miss Darrow .

489
00:36:50,874 --> 00:36:53,714
Aye , aye .

490
00:36:53,865 --> 00:36:57,505
- Ann . Oh , Ann . Did you see her ? - No .

491
00:36:57,692 --> 00:36:59,532
I 'll look below .

492
00:37:04,552 --> 00:37:06,672
- Did you find her ? - Can 't find her forward .

493
00:37:06,824 --> 00:37:09,104
- She 's not below . - Can 't find her aft .

494
00:37:09,296 --> 00:37:10,496
Ann 's gone !

495
00:37:11,610 --> 00:37:14,450
Serve out the rifles . Man the boats .

496
00:37:15,756 --> 00:37:17,996
Take this ammunition outside .

497
00:37:18,148 --> 00:37:19,908
Come on , you fellas . Grab these guns .

498
00:37:20,103 --> 00:37:22,863
Take these bomb cases and be careful with them .

499
00:37:23,135 --> 00:37:25,335
Pass those rifles up over the side .

500
00:37:27,960 --> 00:37:29,920
Start packing those bombs .

501
00:37:30,550 --> 00:37:32,510
Me likey go too . Me likey catch missy .

502
00:37:32,665 --> 00:37:35,705
This is no job for a cook . Get out of here . Come on .

503
00:37:36,453 --> 00:37:38,533
Shove her off , men . We 're going over the side .

504
00:37:39,205 --> 00:37:41,605
Give way , gentlemen . Right over there .

505
00:37:41,756 --> 00:37:43,316
They 've taken Ann .

506
00:43:50,224 --> 00:43:54,064
Hurry . Hurry up . She must be up ahead here .

507
00:43:54,210 --> 00:43:55,810
- Come on , men . - Come on , boys .

508
00:43:55,966 --> 00:43:57,566
Has anybody seen her ? Come on .

509
00:44:23,881 --> 00:44:25,161
Get this gate open . Quick !

510
00:44:25,794 --> 00:44:28,554
Get up there , men . Pull that thing back !

511
00:44:28,705 --> 00:44:30,985
Pull that bar back . He 's got Ann .

512
00:44:31,178 --> 00:44:33,898
Heave . Heave .

513
00:44:35,005 --> 00:44:37,405
Heave . Heave .

514
00:44:37,557 --> 00:44:39,397
- Who 's going with me ? - I 'll go .

515
00:44:46,132 --> 00:44:48,452
You stay with half the men and guard the gate .

516
00:44:48,604 --> 00:44:51,124
- Don 't let them close it . - We 'll take care of it .

517
00:45:34,026 --> 00:45:36,666
No telling which way he went in this darkness .

518
00:45:36,817 --> 00:45:38,177
He 's been through here .

519
00:45:38,372 --> 00:45:41,812
- Look at these broken branches . - Yeah , look at that . Keep up , fellas .

520
00:45:43,515 --> 00:45:45,435
It ought to be sunup about now .

521
00:45:45,589 --> 00:45:48,669
Yeah , just listen to those birds .

522
00:45:48,819 --> 00:45:51,139
It 's dawn all right .

523
00:45:51,291 --> 00:45:54,611
- What 's that ? - Holy mackerel !

524
00:45:54,761 --> 00:45:57,481
Yeah , that 's his track . Look at the size of that thing .

525
00:45:57,672 --> 00:45:59,192
He must be as big as a house .

526
00:45:59,347 --> 00:46:00,707
He 's headed this way .

527
00:46:00,862 --> 00:46:03,262
Come on , fellas , and keep those guns cocked .

528
00:46:03,455 --> 00:46:05,415
Hate to have that thing wrapped around me .

529
00:46:14,141 --> 00:46:16,341
Here 's another one . We 're on his trail .

530
00:46:16,534 --> 00:46:19,734
Sure , sure . I know that . Come on . Come on , fellas .

531
00:46:24,350 --> 00:46:26,110
Hey , look at that !

532
00:46:27,182 --> 00:46:29,702
Keep quiet . He doesn 't see us .

533
00:46:36,433 --> 00:46:38,633
Give me one of those bombs .

534
00:46:51,627 --> 00:46:53,747
Look , it 's gonna charge .

535
00:47:01,437 --> 00:47:03,357
Keep quiet .

536
00:47:07,617 --> 00:47:09,177
Come on .

537
00:47:27,716 --> 00:47:29,516
Give him another one .

538
00:47:33,019 --> 00:47:34,339
Look out !

539
00:47:54,513 --> 00:47:57,073
Look out . He 's still alive .

540
00:47:57,325 --> 00:47:59,045
Shoot .

541
00:48:05,420 --> 00:48:07,460
Come on . That got him .

542
00:48:13,755 --> 00:48:15,315
What do you call this thing ?

543
00:48:15,509 --> 00:48:18,149
Why , something from the dinosaur family .

544
00:48:18,341 --> 00:48:20,141
Dinosaur , eh ?

545
00:48:20,295 --> 00:48:21,815
Yes , Jack

546
00:48:22,008 --> 00:48:24,568
a prehistoric beast .

547
00:48:27,870 --> 00:48:31,350
Say , just look at the length of that brute .

548
00:48:33,214 --> 00:48:36,494
If I could only bring back one of these alive .

549
00:48:36,644 --> 00:48:40,244
- Watch that tail ! He 's still alive . - Come on , looks like he 's standing up .

550
00:48:40,433 --> 00:48:42,593
He 's through . Come on .

551
00:48:42,746 --> 00:48:45,586
Come on , men .

552
00:48:47,929 --> 00:48:50,009
Boy , one swipe of that .

553
00:49:05,476 --> 00:49:07,036
- Hear that ? - Yeah . What is it ?

554
00:49:07,189 --> 00:49:09,349
That 's him , boys . Come on .

555
00:49:22,622 --> 00:49:25,422
Here . Here 's his mark again .

556
00:49:26,013 --> 00:49:29,013
- There 's water ahead . - He 's down in that fog somewhere .

557
00:49:30,638 --> 00:49:32,718
Yes , that 's him splashing through . Come on .

558
00:49:32,872 --> 00:49:34,192
Be careful .

559
00:49:40,808 --> 00:49:44,368
Now , watch the step-off , boys .

560
00:49:44,517 --> 00:49:45,837
Must have swum across .

561
00:49:46,031 --> 00:49:49,191
Yeah , it 'll be tough for us with these guns and bombs .

562
00:49:49,340 --> 00:49:51,820
- What about these logs for a raft ? - Good idea .

563
00:49:52,013 --> 00:49:53,333
Come , fellas . Get busy .

564
00:49:53,489 --> 00:49:56,649
Put those guns down on the bank and get going .

565
00:49:58,434 --> 00:49:59,874
Move !

566
00:50:00,029 --> 00:50:01,829
Come on with those poles .

567
00:50:01,984 --> 00:50:04,104
All set , everybody ?

568
00:50:05,093 --> 00:50:06,813
Shove off !

569
00:50:29,338 --> 00:50:32,938
- Hear anything ? - No , he 's miles away by now .

570
00:50:33,088 --> 00:50:36,128
We 'll be able to pick up his trail all right .

571
00:50:48,719 --> 00:50:50,119
Listen .

572
00:51:03,713 --> 00:51:05,393
Quiet .

573
00:51:08,618 --> 00:51:10,378
What was it ?

574
00:51:22,814 --> 00:51:24,694
Hang on , men .

575
00:51:33,740 --> 00:51:36,260
Look out . Here he comes .

576
00:52:52,817 --> 00:52:54,577
Come on .

577
00:54:29,879 --> 00:54:31,799
Come on .

578
01:01:27,078 --> 01:01:30,278
Hey , Jack . Jack Driscoll .

579
01:01:30,468 --> 01:01:32,908
- Hey , Jack . - Denham .

580
01:01:33,060 --> 01:01:35,860
- It didn 't get you , huh ? - No , I got to cover , same as you .

581
01:01:36,012 --> 01:01:37,932
- Think we 're safe ? - There are two of us

582
01:01:38,125 --> 01:01:41,085
left alive to save her . - I can 't get across now .

583
01:01:41,235 --> 01:01:43,515
Don 't want you to . Lam back and get more bombs .

584
01:01:43,946 --> 01:01:46,426
Why , you wouldn 't follow that beast alone .

585
01:01:46,578 --> 01:01:48,698
Someone 's gotta stay on his trail .

586
01:01:48,892 --> 01:01:50,492
I 'll get a chance , sneak her away .

587
01:01:50,646 --> 01:01:53,326
I 'll figure a way to signal you where he 's taken her .

588
01:01:53,558 --> 01:01:57,118
- I guess that 's our only out . - Sure it is . Get going .

589
01:01:57,306 --> 01:01:59,506
Don 't get killed till you see Englehorn .

590
01:01:59,658 --> 01:02:01,298
Okay , Jack . Good luck .

591
01:03:31,735 --> 01:03:34,215
Skipper , this Kong is the biggest thing in the world .

592
01:03:34,406 --> 01:03:36,886
He shook those men off that log like they were flies .

593
01:03:37,039 --> 01:03:40,719
All those men lost . It 's incredible .

594
01:03:40,867 --> 01:03:43,427
Driscoll said he 'd try and signal us if he found Ann .

595
01:03:43,579 --> 01:03:46,019
- We 'll never see them again . - Don 't give up .

596
01:03:46,171 --> 01:03:48,611
- There 's chance for Driscoll . - Wait for daylight .

597
01:03:48,764 --> 01:03:51,244
We 'll bridge the ravine . Where 's that case of bombs ?

598
01:03:51,395 --> 01:03:53,035
- Here , sir . - This ...

599
01:03:53,188 --> 01:03:56,628
This monster you 've seen , you think your bombs will stop him ?

600
01:03:56,778 --> 01:04:00,058
If we can get close enough to use them , you bet they 'll stop him .

601
01:04:00,207 --> 01:04:02,927
- Had any trouble with the natives ? - Yes , after you left .

602
01:04:03,119 --> 01:04:05,079
- What happened ? - We fired volleys over

603
01:04:05,232 --> 01:04:07,312
their heads , they ran like rabbits .

604
01:04:07,465 --> 01:04:08,985
Gunpowder 's new in their lives ?

605
01:04:09,180 --> 01:04:11,180
- They 're terrified . - They haven 't shown up .

606
01:04:11,373 --> 01:04:13,653
Take a man on the wall , keep your eyes peeled .

607
01:04:13,806 --> 01:04:15,966
We leave at dawn , if we get a signal or not .

608
01:04:16,118 --> 01:04:17,398
Yes , sir .

609
01:13:19,151 --> 01:13:20,911
Hey , look .

610
01:13:26,328 --> 01:13:29,208
Hey , below , Mr. Denham . Captain Englehorn .

611
01:13:29,359 --> 01:13:31,959
Mr. Driscoll and the lady , they 're coming back .

612
01:13:32,110 --> 01:13:34,350
Come on , fellas .

613
01:13:38,730 --> 01:13:40,330
Are you both all right ?

614
01:13:40,525 --> 01:13:41,965
Pint , Jack . Here .

615
01:13:46,427 --> 01:13:48,587
I 'm all right .

616
01:13:48,780 --> 01:13:50,740
What happened ? How did you do it ?

617
01:13:50,931 --> 01:13:52,931
- Came down the river . - Oh , Jack .

618
01:13:53,284 --> 01:13:55,684
There , there , you 're safe now .

619
01:13:55,837 --> 01:13:58,557
We 'll have you back on the ship in no time .

620
01:14:02,218 --> 01:14:04,098
Wait a minute . What about Kong ?

621
01:14:04,252 --> 01:14:06,212
Well , what about him ?

622
01:14:08,041 --> 01:14:10,761
We came to get a movie , and we found something worth

623
01:14:10,911 --> 01:14:13,231
more than all the movies in the world . - What ?

624
01:14:13,543 --> 01:14:14,943
We 've got those gas bombs .

625
01:14:15,099 --> 01:14:18,219
- Lf we can capture him alive ... - Why , you 're crazy .

626
01:14:18,408 --> 01:14:20,408
He 's on a cliff where a whole army

627
01:14:20,601 --> 01:14:23,881
couldn 't get at him . - Yeah , if he stays there

628
01:14:24,071 --> 01:14:26,871
but we 've got something he wants .

629
01:14:27,061 --> 01:14:29,981
Yeah , something he won 't get again .

630
01:14:30,371 --> 01:14:33,451
Hey , look out . It 's Kong . Kong 's coming .

631
01:14:58,407 --> 01:15:01,167
Come around . Come here and hold the gates . Quick .

632
01:15:01,356 --> 01:15:04,836
- Denham , natives are coming . - Good work . Come on .

633
01:16:55,326 --> 01:16:57,726
Hey , come back with those bombs , you ...

634
01:19:39,502 --> 01:19:42,662
Come on . Come on . I got him .

635
01:19:44,327 --> 01:19:46,207
He 'll be out for hours . Send to the ship .

636
01:19:46,480 --> 01:19:48,840
- For anchor chains and tools . - What will you do ?

637
01:19:49,034 --> 01:19:52,514
A raft to float him to the ship . The whole world will pay to see this .

638
01:19:52,662 --> 01:19:55,662
- No chains will hold that . - We 'll give him more than chains .

639
01:19:55,851 --> 01:19:59,011
He 's always been king of his world , but we 'll teach him fear .

640
01:19:59,161 --> 01:20:02,041
We 're millionaires , boys . I 'll share it with all of you .

641
01:20:02,191 --> 01:20:04,831
In a few months , it 'll be up in lights on Broadway :

642
01:20:04,984 --> 01:20:08,944
" Kong , the Eighth Wonder of the World . "

643
01:20:27,434 --> 01:20:28,994
Say , what 's Denham got anyway ?

644
01:20:29,149 --> 01:20:31,749
It better be good after all this ballyhoo .

645
01:20:31,941 --> 01:20:34,061
Heavens , what a mob .

646
01:20:34,213 --> 01:20:38,093
Well , you would come . These tickets cost me 20 bucks .

647
01:20:47,253 --> 01:20:50,613
I can 't sit so near the screen . It hurts my eyes .

648
01:20:50,803 --> 01:20:52,483
This is not a moving picture , madam .

649
01:20:52,755 --> 01:20:55,235
What ? Mr. Denham makes those pictures

650
01:20:55,429 --> 01:20:58,789
of those darling monkeys and tigers and things .

651
01:20:58,937 --> 01:21:01,377
This is in the nature of a personal appearance .

652
01:21:01,530 --> 01:21:05,010
Well , I never . I thought I was gonna see something .

653
01:21:05,437 --> 01:21:08,637
- Say , what is it anyhow ? - I hear it 's a kind of a gorilla .

654
01:21:08,788 --> 01:21:11,588
Gee , ain 't we got enough of them in New York ?

655
01:21:17,361 --> 01:21:18,841
I don 't like to look at him .

656
01:21:18,996 --> 01:21:21,556
It makes me think of that awful day on the island .

657
01:21:21,906 --> 01:21:25,266
I wouldn 't have brought you , but you know how Denham insisted .

658
01:21:25,416 --> 01:21:27,936
We had to come when he said it would help the show .

659
01:21:28,128 --> 01:21:30,168
Do you think we 'll make a lot of money ?

660
01:21:30,321 --> 01:21:33,361
Well , enough to pay him back for these clothes anyway .

661
01:21:33,550 --> 01:21:37,030
It 's the first time I ever had on one of these open-front suits .

662
01:21:37,181 --> 01:21:40,021
Hello , there . Just in time . Gee , Ann , you look great .

663
01:21:40,171 --> 01:21:44,771
I 'm glad I dressed you up for this show . Well , Jack , $ 10,000 in the box office .

664
01:21:44,956 --> 01:21:47,356
- Not bad for one night . - That 's a lot of money .

665
01:21:47,508 --> 01:21:49,188
We 're gonna do that every night .

666
01:21:49,782 --> 01:21:52,982
- Look at the size of that . - I hope he 's tied up tight .

667
01:21:53,131 --> 01:21:55,491
Sure he is . Denham 's taking no chances .

668
01:21:55,644 --> 01:21:57,604
Here are the press . Come in , boys .

669
01:21:57,757 --> 01:22:00,237
- This is Ms. Darrow and Mr. Driscoll . - How do you do ?

670
01:22:00,430 --> 01:22:02,350
Mr. Driscoll saved you from the ape ?

671
01:22:02,502 --> 01:22:06,062
Yes . He was alone too . All the sailors with him had been killed .

672
01:22:06,211 --> 01:22:09,811
- How did you ever tackle that baby ? - Well , Mr. Denham got him .

673
01:22:09,999 --> 01:22:12,079
The rest of us were running scared .

674
01:22:12,233 --> 01:22:14,553
He had the nerve to stand there and chuck bombs .

675
01:22:14,704 --> 01:22:17,224
Oh , so you 're the hero . Come on , give us a story .

676
01:22:17,377 --> 01:22:19,657
Here now , wait a minute . Lay off me , boys .

677
01:22:19,849 --> 01:22:22,449
Miss Darrow is the story . If it hadn 't been for her

678
01:22:22,600 --> 01:22:25,480
we couldn 't have gotten near Kong . He followed her .

679
01:22:25,631 --> 01:22:27,791
- Beauty and the beast , huh ? - That 's it .

680
01:22:27,944 --> 01:22:30,144
Play up that angle , beauty and the beast .

681
01:22:30,297 --> 01:22:32,097
Kong could have stayed safe

682
01:22:32,289 --> 01:22:34,249
but he couldn 't stay away from beauty .

683
01:22:34,443 --> 01:22:37,203
- That 's your story , boys . - That 's a lead story , all right .

684
01:22:37,355 --> 01:22:39,315
- How about some pictures ? - Just a minute .

685
01:22:39,509 --> 01:22:42,349
Come on the stage . Take pictures in front of the audience .

686
01:22:42,499 --> 01:22:45,019
I 'll make a speech and tell them about Kong , Darrow

687
01:22:45,170 --> 01:22:47,770
Driscoll . When I call you , come take pictures .

688
01:22:47,962 --> 01:22:49,522
- Okay . - That 's fine .

689
01:22:49,717 --> 01:22:51,317
Stand by , Ann , when I call you .

690
01:22:51,471 --> 01:22:52,951
Now , now , it 's all right .

691
01:22:53,108 --> 01:22:56,188
We 've knocked some of the fight out of him since you saw him .

692
01:23:12,168 --> 01:23:16,408
Ladies and gentlemen , I am here tonight to tell you a very strange story .

693
01:23:16,594 --> 01:23:19,474
A story so strange that no one will believe it .

694
01:23:19,984 --> 01:23:23,064
But , ladies and gentlemen , seeing is believing

695
01:23:23,255 --> 01:23:25,055
and we , my partners and I

696
01:23:25,208 --> 01:23:27,808
have brought back the living proof of our adventure .

697
01:23:27,959 --> 01:23:31,919
... an adventure in which 12 of our party met horrible deaths .

698
01:23:32,187 --> 01:23:35,307
And now , ladies and gentlemen , before I tell you any more

699
01:23:35,535 --> 01:23:38,775
I am going to show you the greatest thing your eyes ever beheld .

700
01:23:39,126 --> 01:23:42,486
He was a king and a god in the world he knew

701
01:23:42,674 --> 01:23:46,474
but now he comes to civilization merely a captive

702
01:23:46,622 --> 01:23:49,262
a show to gratify your curiosity .

703
01:23:49,370 --> 01:23:52,770
Ladies and gentlemen , look at Kong .

704
01:23:52,959 --> 01:23:54,799
The Eighth Wonder of the World .

705
01:24:13,217 --> 01:24:15,937
And now I want to introduce Miss Ann Darrow

706
01:24:16,088 --> 01:24:19,048
the bravest girl I have ever known .

707
01:24:29,527 --> 01:24:32,127
There the beast and here the beauty .

708
01:24:32,279 --> 01:24:35,839
She has lived through an experience no other woman ever dreamed of .

709
01:24:35,987 --> 01:24:40,667
And she was saved from the very grasp of Kong by her future husband .

710
01:24:40,814 --> 01:24:44,974
I want you to meet a very brave gentleman , Mr. John Driscoll .

711
01:24:55,806 --> 01:24:58,726
And now before I tell you the full story of our voyage

712
01:24:58,918 --> 01:25:01,838
I will ask the gentlemen of the press to come forward

713
01:25:01,987 --> 01:25:05,507
so that the audience may see them take the first photographs

714
01:25:05,695 --> 01:25:08,535
of Kong and his captors .

715
01:25:08,686 --> 01:25:10,326
All right , boys .

716
01:25:15,506 --> 01:25:19,466
Miss Darrow first , alone . Stand in front of Kong , Ann .

717
01:25:23,961 --> 01:25:25,881
- All set ? Make it a good one . - Okay .

718
01:25:26,034 --> 01:25:27,354
Shoot .

719
01:25:34,607 --> 01:25:39,087
Don 't be alarmed . Those chains are made of chrome steel .

720
01:25:43,620 --> 01:25:45,900
- It 's all right , Ann . - Get them together , boys .

721
01:25:45,892 --> 01:25:49,332
- They 're going to be married tomorrow . - Put your arm around her , Driscoll .

722
01:25:52,113 --> 01:25:53,393
Wait a minute . Hold on .

723
01:25:53,549 --> 01:25:56,749
- He thinks you 're attacking the girl . - All the roaring , swell picture .

724
01:26:05,651 --> 01:26:06,971
Come on , it 's loose !

725
01:26:57,931 --> 01:27:01,091
Send the riot squad and ambulances . Kong has escaped .

726
01:28:09,710 --> 01:28:11,190
You 're safe now , dear .

727
01:28:11,903 --> 01:28:14,303
It 's like a horrible dream .

728
01:28:15,291 --> 01:28:17,451
It 's like being back on the island again .

729
01:28:17,605 --> 01:28:20,405
Now , it 's all right . Don 't worry .

730
01:28:20,556 --> 01:28:23,036
I 'm gonna stay right here with you .

731
01:28:23,188 --> 01:28:25,908
Anyhow , you know they 're bound to get him .

732
01:29:25,037 --> 01:29:26,797
Jack , he 's climbing up outside there .

733
01:29:26,752 --> 01:29:29,152
- He 's got Ann . He 's taken her up . - The roof , quick .

734
01:30:33,786 --> 01:30:35,466
Ann , Ann !

735
01:30:35,619 --> 01:30:38,619
How can we follow him ? What 'll we do ?

736
01:30:38,770 --> 01:30:41,170
Fire department searchlights on the roof .

737
01:30:41,323 --> 01:30:43,683
Yeah , they 'll keep him in sight .

738
01:32:29,790 --> 01:32:32,830
Attention all stations . Kong is going west .

739
01:32:32,980 --> 01:32:35,180
He is making for the Empire State Building .

740
01:32:35,374 --> 01:32:37,934
Stand by for further reports .

741
01:32:38,084 --> 01:32:41,364
- Lf he goes up there , what can we do ? - We won 't get near him .

742
01:32:41,792 --> 01:32:44,072
Kong is climbing the Empire State Building .

743
01:32:44,226 --> 01:32:46,906
He is still carrying Ann Darrow . That is all .

744
01:32:47,057 --> 01:32:48,817
That licks us .

745
01:32:49,092 --> 01:32:50,892
- One thing we haven 't thought of . - What ?

746
01:32:51,044 --> 01:32:53,244
Airplanes . If he should put Ann down

747
01:32:53,437 --> 01:32:55,717
and they fly close to pick him without her ...

748
01:32:55,870 --> 01:32:57,390
You 're right . Planes .

749
01:32:57,584 --> 01:32:59,264
Call the field .

750
01:33:32,636 --> 01:33:35,476
- Here come the planes . - They 'll get him .

751
01:33:38,060 --> 01:33:40,940
- Can they shoot him and not hit Ann ? - They 'll be shooting .

752
01:38:22,623 --> 01:38:25,823
Ann . Ann , hang on , dear .

753
01:38:26,012 --> 01:38:29,092
- Ann , are you all right ? - Jack !

754
01:38:45,752 --> 01:38:47,472
Just a moment . Wait a minute .

755
01:38:47,664 --> 01:38:49,504
Let me through . My name is Denham .

756
01:38:49,699 --> 01:38:52,059
Just a moment . Oh , lieutenant .

757
01:38:52,212 --> 01:38:54,972
- Lieutenant , I 'm Carl Denham . - Carl Denham .

758
01:38:55,123 --> 01:38:57,843
Denham ? Oh , that 's the man that captured the monster .

759
01:39:00,865 --> 01:39:04,505
Well , Denham , the airplanes got him .

760
01:39:06,088 --> 01:39:09,528
Oh , no , it wasn 't the airplanes .

761
01:39:09,679 --> 01:39:12,759
It was beauty killed the beast .

762
01:39:47,960 --> 01:39:49,960
[ ENGLISH ]

